# Text files: detected automatically, stored and checked out with LF endings.
# "text=auto" rather than a bare "text" matters. Setting it outright declares
# every file in the repository to be text, which overrides Git's own detection
# and strips CR bytes out of binaries as they are committed. Nothing complains:
# the file is compared after that same normalisation, so it reads as unchanged
# while what is stored no longer matches what is on disk.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Project Zomboid reads these as plain text. Item scripts, recipes, translation
# files and mod.info are all line based, and the game is happy with LF.
*.lua text eol=lf
*.txt text eol=lf
*.info text eol=lf
*.xml text eol=lf

# LF everywhere, PowerShell included. pwsh reads LF scripts without complaint, and
# a single ending across the repo means no file ever shows as wholly changed just
# because it was opened on a different machine.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=lf

# Binaries, kept byte for byte. Auto-detection already covers these; naming them
# is the belt to its braces, since the failure is silent and only shows up in a
# fresh clone. Vehicle models and part textures are the ones that actually
# matter here.
*.fbx binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.psd binary
*.ico binary
*.zip binary
*.class binary
